---
import Layout from '../../layouts/Layout.astro';

const paper = {
  title: "Delegation in the Age of Agentic AI",
  subtitle: "Authority, Access, On-Behalf-Of Execution, and Identity Impersonation",
  date: "July 2026",
  version: "2.0",
  author: "Jan Uyttenhove",
  pdfHref: "/papers/delegation-in-the-age-of-agentic-ai.pdf",
  tags: ["agentic AI", "delegation", "identity", "zero trust", "IAM", "governance"],
};

const sections = [
  "Executive Overview",
  "Conceptual Definitions",
  "Unified Structural Comparison",
  "The Agentic AI Paradigm Shift",
  "Security Threat Modeling and Governance Architecture",
  "Conclusion and Future Outlook",
  "References",
];

const linkedInProfile = 'https://be.linkedin.com/in/januyttenhove';
---

<Layout title={`${paper.title} - Insidin`} description={`${paper.subtitle}. A paper by ${paper.author} on delegation and identity in agentic AI.`}>
  <section class="pt-32 pb-24 px-6">
    <div class="max-w-3xl mx-auto">
      <!-- Breadcrumb -->
      <div class="inline-flex items-center gap-2 mb-6">
        <a href="/papers" class="mono-xs text-muted hover:text-accent transition-colors">Papers</a>
        <span class="mono-xs text-border">/</span>
        <span class="mono-xs text-accent">Delegation in the Age of Agentic AI</span>
      </div>

      <!-- Header -->
      <h1 class="d-l text-primary mb-2" style="font-size:clamp(1.6rem,3.5vw,2.2rem)">{paper.title}</h1>
      <p class="b-l text-muted mb-6">{paper.subtitle}</p>

      <div class="flex items-center gap-3 flex-wrap mb-8">
        <span class="mono-xs text-muted">{paper.author}</span>
        <span class="text-border">|</span>
        <span class="mono-xs text-muted">{paper.date}</span>
        <span class="text-border">|</span>
        <span class="mono-xs text-muted">Version {paper.version}</span>
      </div>

      <!-- Download button -->
      <div class="flex items-center gap-4 p-5 bg-surface mb-10" style="border-radius:var(--radius-sm)">
        <div class="w-12 h-12 bg-white flex items-center justify-center shrink-0 border border-border" style="border-radius:var(--radius-sm)">
          <svg class="w-6 h-6 text-accent" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" viewBox="0 0 24 24" stroke-width="1.5">
            <path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" d="M19.5 14.25v-2.625a3.375 3.375 0 0 0-3.375-3.375h-1.5A1.125 1.125 0 0 1 13.5 7.125v-1.5a3.375 3.375 0 0 0-3.375-3.375H8.25m2.25 0H5.625c-.621 0-1.125.504-1.125 1.125v17.25c0 .621.504 1.125 1.125 1.125h12.75c.621 0 1.125-.504 1.125-1.125V11.25a9 9 0 0 0-9-9Z" />
          </svg>
        </div>
        <div class="flex-1">
          <p class="d-s text-primary">Download the full paper</p>
          <p class="mono-xs text-muted mt-0.5">PDF, 20+ pages</p>
        </div>
        <a
          href={paper.pdfHref}
          target="_blank"
          class="inline-flex items-center gap-2 px-5 py-2.5 bg-primary text-white text-sm font-semibold hover:opacity-90 transition-opacity"
          style="border-radius:var(--radius-sm)"
        >
          <svg class="w-4 h-4" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" viewBox="0 0 24 24" stroke-width="2">
            <path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" d="M3 16.5v2.25A2.25 2.25 0 0 0 5.25 21h13.5A2.25 2.25 0 0 0 21 18.75V16.5M16.5 12 12 16.5m0 0L7.5 12m4.5 4.5V3" />
          </svg>
          Download PDF
        </a>
      </div>

      <!-- Abstract -->
      <div class="prose mb-10">
        <h2>Abstract</h2>
        <p>
          Agentic AI exposes a gap between authenticating a principal, authorizing a resource operation, and authorizing the business decision that motivates that operation. This paper distinguishes four frequently conflated concepts: Delegation of Authority (the right to decide), Delegation of Access (the right to use resources), On Behalf Of execution (represented action with dual attribution), and Delegation of Identity (impersonation with substituted attribution).
        </p>
        <p>
          Their separation becomes critical in agent-to-agent interactions, where runtime behavior can evolve independently of the permissions initially granted. The paper proposes a zero-trust agent framework combining explicit mandates, independently authenticated workloads, mediated capability acquisition, and verifiable execution records.
        </p>
        <p>
          Its central thesis: safe agentic delegation requires an enforceable relationship among who authorized the task, who performed the action, which operations were permitted, and which business outcomes were authorized.
        </p>
      </div>

      <!-- Table of contents -->
      <div class="p-5 bg-surface mb-10" style="border-radius:var(--radius-sm)">
        <p class="d-s text-primary mb-3">In this paper</p>
        <ol class="space-y-1.5">
          {sections.map((section, i) => (
            <li class="b-s text-muted" style="padding-left:0.5rem">
              <span class="mono-xs text-border mr-2">{String(i + 1).padStart(2, '0')}</span>
              {section}
            </li>
          ))}
        </ol>
      </div>

      <!-- Tags -->
      <div class="flex items-center gap-2 flex-wrap mb-10">
        {paper.tags.map(tag => (
          <span class="mono-xs px-2.5 py-1 bg-surface text-muted" style="border-radius:9999px;font-size:0.6rem">{tag}</span>
        ))}
      </div>

      <!-- Second download CTA -->
      <div class="text-center py-10 border-t border-border">
        <p class="d-m text-primary mb-2">Read the full paper</p>
        <p class="b-s text-muted mb-5">Covering the formal comparison, threat model, zero-trust agent framework, and recommendations for enterprise architects.</p>
        <a
          href={paper.pdfHref}
          target="_blank"
          class="inline-flex items-center gap-2 px-6 py-3 bg-primary text-white text-sm font-semibold hover:opacity-90 transition-opacity"
          style="border-radius:var(--radius-sm)"
        >
          <svg class="w-4 h-4" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" viewBox="0 0 24 24" stroke-width="2">
            <path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" d="M3 16.5v2.25A2.25 2.25 0 0 0 5.25 21h13.5A2.25 2.25 0 0 0 21 18.75V16.5M16.5 12 12 16.5m0 0L7.5 12m4.5 4.5V3" />
          </svg>
          Download PDF
        </a>
      </div>

      <!-- Contact -->
      <div class="flex items-center gap-3 mt-6 p-4 bg-surface" style="border-radius:var(--radius-sm)">
        <svg class="w-5 h-5 text-muted shrink-0" fill="currentColor" viewBox="0 0 24 24">
          <path d="M20.447 20.452h-3.554v-5.569c0-1.328-.027-3.037-1.852-3.037-1.853 0-2.136 1.445-2.136 2.939v5.667H9.351V9h3.414v1.561h.046c.477-.9 1.637-1.85 3.37-1.85 3.601 0 4.267 2.37 4.267 5.455v6.286zM5.337 7.433a2.062 2.062 0 01-2.063-2.065 2.064 2.064 0 112.063 2.065zm1.782 13.019H3.555V9h3.564v11.452zM22.225 0H1.771C.792 0 0 .774 0 1.729v20.542C0 23.227.792 24 1.771 24h20.451C23.2 24 24 23.227 24 22.271V1.729C24 .774 23.2 0 22.222 0h.003z"/>
        </svg>
        <p class="b-s text-muted">
          Questions or feedback? Reach out to
          <a href={linkedInProfile} target="_blank" rel="noopener" class="d-s text-primary hover:text-accent transition-colors">Jan Uyttenhove</a>
          on LinkedIn or via
          <a href="mailto:jan@insidin.com" class="d-s text-primary hover:text-accent transition-colors">jan@insidin.com</a>.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</Layout>
